    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "ea3a66da1fcdfa2db2fc7fe49400a2928a96a165",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1725 \u2014 the card pays what the fight pays\n\nAudit item F3, and it is the same defect as OTA-1708 wearing different clothes.\n\n\u26a0\u26a0\u26a0 THE ITEM CARD READ ONE FIELD AND THE FIGHT READ ANOTHER. `previewArmor`\nprinted `a.statBonus` \u2014 the single legacy field \u2014 while `effectiveStats` sums\n`statBonuses ?? (statBonus ? [statBonus] : [])`. Two different rules over two\nfields that disagree on most of the catalog, so the card was not a summary of\nthe piece; it was a summary of a field.\n\nMEASURED OVER ALL 288 STAT-BEARING ARMOUR ROWS:\n\n    repeat the primary inside statBonuses ......... 204\n    REPLACE it with something else ................  54\n    rows hiding at least one paid bonus .......... 185\n\nThe Aetheric Crown of the Giants grants CHA+3, STR+2 and HP+40. The card said\n\"CHA +3\". The Reclaimer's Salvage Cap authors `statBonus: wisdom+1` and grants\n`investigation+1` \u2014 the card named a stat the fight does not pay at all.\n\nAfter, from the same rows:\n\n    Crown ......... AC +4 \u00b7 Resists: aetheric, slashing, cold \u00b7 CHA +3 \u00b7 STR +2\n                    \u00b7 HP +40 \u00b7 Regen: +1 stamina per action \u00b7 Durability: 65\n    Salvage Cap ... AC +1 \u00b7 INT +1 \u00b7 Durability: 20\n    rows that PAY something 288 \u00b7 still hiding a paid bonus 0\n\n\u26a0\u26a0 ONE AUTHORITY, NOT A THIRD FORMATTER. The either/or expression was written\nout THREE times in equipment.ts and a FOURTH, different rule lived in the\npreview. Adding a fifth would have been the actual bug again. `armorBonusList`\nis the expression, once; `armorPaidBonuses` is the half the game actually pays;\nthe engine summation, `armorHpBonus` and the card all read the same function, so\nthe card cannot promise what the fight does not grant.\n\n\u26a0 AND IT CANNOT OVER-PROMISE EITHER. `add()` filters to STAT_KEYS and hp is paid\nthrough hpMax, so a `constitution` / `acrobatics` / `aetheria` entry has no\nPlayerCharacter field and grants nothing. `armorPaidBonuses` drops those, so the\ncard errs in neither direction. My first pass printed the raw label and produced\n\"INV +1\" for a row that canonicalises to intelligence; it goes through\n`canonicalStatKey` now, so the card names the stat the sheet will show.\n\n\u26a0 ACCESSORIES DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED. `previewAccessory` UNIONS the two fields,\nwhich is a different rule \u2014 and the right one there: of 42 accessory rows 39 are\nsingle-only, and the 3 multi rows EXCLUDE the primary rather than repeating it.\nApplying the armour rule would have deleted a bonus from each of those three.\nTwo catalogs, two authoring conventions, measured separately. Collapsing them to\none function would have been tidier and wrong.\n\n\u26a0 `??` IS EITHER/OR, NOT A UNION \u2014 for the third time now (OTA-1708, OTA-1725,\nand the mistake this OTA nearly made). A union here would have doubled 204 rows\nand resurrected 54 retired values.\n\nFull surface clean: 1185 suites, 12323 tests, 0 failures. 18 gates green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-06T23:52:50Z",
